  "blocks": [
   {
    "id": "p1",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "In the summer of 2025, the film based on Ma Boyong’s novel "
     },
     {
      "t": "em",
      "v": "The Litchi Road"
     },
     {
      "t": "gloss",
      "v": "",
      "zh": "《长安的荔枝》"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " became a big "
     },
     {
      "t": "vocab",
      "v": "hit",
      "ref": "v-hit"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " in China. In just four days, it earned more than 258 million "
     },
     {
      "t": "em",
      "v": "yuan"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " at the box office. The writer behind it, Ma Boyong, is famous for "
     },
     {
      "t": "vocab",
      "v": "blending",
      "ref": "v-blend"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " history with storytelling."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p2",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Ma, now 46, has sold millions of books. He often finds "
     },
     {
      "t": "vocab",
      "v": "inspiration",
      "ref": "v-inspiration"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " in small details of history. Once, at a museum, he saw "
     },
     {
      "t": "gloss",
      "v": "bamboo slips",
      "zh": "竹简"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " listing daily jobs, like how many rats people had to catch. Most visitors might see them as simple records, but Ma saw a starting point for stories. He enjoys bringing these little pieces of history to life for modern readers."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p3",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "In "
     },
     {
      "t": "em",
      "v": "The Litchi Road"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": ", he focused on a Tang poem about lychees. The poem reads, “A "
     },
     {
      "t": "gloss",
      "v": "steed",
      "zh": "坐骑"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " raising red dust won the fair mistress’s smile; no one knew how many steeds carrying lychees died along the way.” Most people remember the image of a smiling "
     },
     {
      "t": "gloss",
      "v": "concubine",
      "zh": "妃子"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": ". But Ma asked a different question: How could fresh lychees travel such a long distance to Chang’an without going bad? To write the novel, he broke this big question into smaller ones, just like a project manager. He studied the roads, the horses, and the methods of transport. Step by step, he solved each part and produced a 70,000-word bestselling novel that combines historical facts with imagination."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p4",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Readers love this blend. One fan said Ma’s books mix "
     },
     {
      "t": "vocab",
      "v": "solid",
      "ref": "v-solid"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " research with humour, making history lively. For Ma, history is not just the past—it connects with the present. He hopes his stories will encourage readers to visit Xi’an, walk along the "
     },
     {
      "t": "gloss",
      "v": "Grand Canal",
      "zh": "大运河"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": ", or even taste fresh lychees."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p5",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "“A novel is like a window,” Ma said. “You catch a "
     },
     {
      "t": "vocab",
      "v": "glimpse",
      "ref": "v-glimpse"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " of the sky, then step out and walk into it.” For many young readers, his works have become that window into history and imagination."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
